    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i used to think everything depended on being the best. like if i wasn't going to be top tier, there was no point in even trying. i just hit this wall today. i realized i'm just... okay. i'll always just be okay. it feels like i've been playing a game for years just to realize i'm a NPC in my own life. what's even the point of grinding through decades of mediocrity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're experiencing a significant shift in perspective, and that feeling of hitting a wall can be deeply discouraging. Please know that \"okay\" is not a failure; it's a starting point for a different kind of fulfillment. Instead of chasing an impossible \"best,\" perhaps you could explore what genuinely brings you satisfaction, even in small moments. Redefining success away from external validation can open up a much more meaningful path forward.",
